# Xen Dynamic Function Tracer Demo

This repository contains an experimental proof of concept for demonstrating
a tracer that can be used like Linux ftrace.

The implementation is based on the following RFC:
https://lists.xenproject.org/archives/html/xen-devel/2026-08/msg00581.html

## Background

Xen already provides many debugging tools. But the existing tools need
the sites of interest to be instrumented. It requires code modification
and rebuilding Xen. This project explores a more dynamic tool for
debugging on Xen inspired by Linux ftrace.

## Design

This project adopts the approach of Linux ftrace.
It prepares compiler-generated patchable function entries and a trampoline.
Xen livepatch is used for the dynamic patching of the entries and HypFS is
used for managing the tracers.

## Limitations

- Arm64 only
- Function-entry tracing only
- Assumes a machine is running on single CPU because patching through
  `register_function_hook()` does not support synchronization across CPUs

## Build configuration

The following Xen configuration options must be enabled:

```text
CONFIG_ARM64_PATCHABLE_FUNCTION_ENTRY=y
CONFIG_HYPFS=y
CONFIG_LIVEPATCH=y
```

## Demo

Tracers are under /tracing directory. The functions available for tracing
can be looked up with /tracing/available_functions.

```sh
xenhypfs tree
xenhypfs cat /tracing/available_functions
```

Select `do_domctl()` and enable tracing:

```sh
xenhypfs write /tracing/function/filter do_domctl
xenhypfs write /tracing/function/enabled 1
xenhypfs cat /tracing/enabled_functions
```

Trigger a call to `do_domctl()` and display the captured trace:

```sh
xl vcpu-list
xenhypfs cat /tracing/function/trace
```

Finally, disable tracing:

```sh
xenhypfs write /tracing/function/enabled 0
xenhypfs cat /tracing/function/enabled
xenhypfs cat /tracing/enabled_functions
```
